{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Who…</b> Some say this coming one is the Messiah, and some say he is Michael, and the correct view is that it is an allusion to the revered Name, and the meaning concerns the decree He decreed upon Edom — and this is the kingdom of Rome and Constantinople, and they are called Edomites because they entered into the religion of Edom, and this religion was named after Edom, for the Edomites initially believed in the Torah of the known man:" "<b>Crimson garments.</b> From the root of חומץ (Numbers 6:3)." "This, that his garments were <b>stained.</b> And the meaning is how they became defiled." "<b>Marching.</b> Others, like ושלחתי לו צועים וצעוהו (Jeremiah 48:12), meaning advancing in great strength. And Rabbi Moses the Kohen, of blessed memory, says that צועה is like מהר צועה להפת (Isaiah 51:14), and it is an epithet of the Name and is not a verb in this context." "<b>And since he said, 'Who is this.'</b> He answered: I speak, mighty to save — רב like על כל רב ביתו (Esther 1:8)." "<b>From Bozrah.</b> A place name, as though he came from there. Now the meaning is from the people of Bozrah, and they are Edom and those who follow their religion in every place they are."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 63, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:00:47.417748383Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}